cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Schema Crush: calibrated semantic schema matching for biomedical data to FHIR"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Nasim
    family-names: Sanati
    email: nasim@plenary.org
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/teslajoy/schema_crush"
abstract: >-
  Schema Crush is a semantic schema matching framework that aligns heterogeneous
  biomedical data schemas to HL7 FHIR R5. It combines rule-based lookup over
  expert-curated mappings, embedding-based semantic similarity (BioBERT,
  Magneto), and isotonic confidence calibration fitted on 1,280 expert mapping
  rules from FHIR Aggregator sources (GDC, HTAN, CDA). An optional LLM agent
  layer resolves uncertain cases using the matchers as tools, with
  human-in-the-loop review and feedback capture. The package also exposes its
  matchers as an MCP server.
keywords:
  - FHIR
  - schema matching
  - biomedical data harmonization
  - ontology mapping
  - confidence calibration
  - BioBERT
  - large language model agents
  - Model Context Protocol
